## Backend Structure Expectations

Future backend code must be modular, not piled into `main.py`:

```
backend-api/app/main.py            # app wiring only
backend-api/app/core/config.py     # settings/env loading
backend-api/app/core/security.py   # password hashing, JWT, RBAC helpers
backend-api/app/db/session.py      # database connection/session management
backend-api/app/api/routes/        # one router module per feature area
backend-api/app/schemas/           # Pydantic request/response models
backend-api/app/services/          # business logic
```

Use parameterized SQL only (no string-formatted queries). Config comes from environment variables only, matching the existing `_env()` helper pattern.

## Communication Rules (the user is not a programmer)

- Explain changes in simple language, always naming the exact file and its full path.
- Provide complete file content or complete edits — never partial snippets, never "add the rest yourself," never `TODO`/placeholder code in production files.
- Provide exact commands and their expected output.
- Never hide a failed command.
- Never make a large architectural change without first explaining it in plain language and getting explicit approval.
- Always show `git status --short` after changes, then stop and wait — do not commit automatically.
